From: richie-rich90454 <rjiang880@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0002/0014] Rebrand runtime strings

This patch replaces user-visible Microsoft, Visual Studio, VS Code,
vscode, github.com/microsoft/vscode, microsoft.com, aka.ms, and
go.microsoft.com references with Jahaziel equivalents.

Rationale: no upstream brand string may reach the user.

Touches:
  - runtime strings across src/, extensions/, resources/ (generated)

Generated by: ide/scripts/rebrand.py. Review the produced diff
before committing this patch; the generator output is the patch body.

Diff: authored on the upstream checkout (see build.sh).
Verification: grep for microsoft/vscode brand strings finds no runtime hit.

---
